{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","level":2,"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction","level":3,"text":"Interaction","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"doc:Interaction_Touch","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Swami","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"Swami","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"pa